{
  "about": "Telnet corpus v1: byte chunks mapped to payload bytes, negotiation replies, echo/MCP state events, and NVT lines.",
  "schema": "Each cases entry feeds chunks (arrays of unsigned bytes) into a fresh filter; data is concatenated payload, replies are negotiation byte arrays, and echo/mcp are state notifications. Each lineCases entry maps chunks to complete NVT lines without terminators. Chunk boundaries must not change results. Policy accepts ECHO and MCP option 70, refuses others; lines recognize CR LF and LF, and CR NUL represents a literal CR.",
  "sources": [
    "toaststunt/src/network.cc:386-470 (IAC framing), 1748-1758 (WILL/WONT ECHO)",
    "web/AGENTS.md: outgoing IAC doubling and server ECHO",
    "web/bouncer/DESIGN.md: bouncer terminates Telnet negotiation"
  ],
